__pycache__/
*.pyc
results/receipts/
results/live/
# Raw ablation rows carry verifier tracebacks with temp paths. The publishable
# artifact is ablation.json, which records every replicate's outcome.
results/ablation/*/runs/
results/screens/*/runs/
# Mutated task instances are generated, not authored. Any instance is
# reproducible from its seed, and committing them would republish the very text
# the mutation exists to keep out of training data.
results/mutants/
# Jobs that were interrupted before they measured anything: a host shutdown, a
# wall-clock ceiling, a kill. They are kept on disk as operational history and
# not published.
#
# The line is between a run and a job. Every replicate of a run that gets
# reported is published, including the ones that failed, because dropping those
# is how a cell gets to look cleaner than it was. A job that was killed at 2 of
# 8 tasks reported nothing to be selective about, and in both current cases the
# same work completed properly in another record. Publishing crashed jobs is not
# more honest, only noisier.
#
# A run that COMPLETED and produced a void or superseded result is published,
# with its irregularity note. That is a finding about the instrument and belongs
# in the record.
results/aborted/
.DS_Store
# Live JSON can include model request ids; keep local-only unless curating a board
# results/live/ is retained on disk for CROSS_STACK_BOARD; do not push secrets
